.TH GENERATE_HTML 1 "2026-07-02" "reta 12c4z" "Reta commands"
.SH NAME
generate_html \- generate the complete Reta HTML document
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B generate_html
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B generate_html
assembles the complete Reta HTML page from the native all-columns table,
the hierarchy section and the installed static assets.  The command does not
start Python or a child Reta process.
.PP
By default the document is written to standard output.  No intermediate file
is created unless explicitly requested.  This makes the command safe for an
FHS installation below
.IR /usr
or
.IR /usr/local
and for execution from arbitrary working directories.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -o " " FILE , " " --output " " FILE
Write the final HTML document atomically to
.IR FILE
instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR -l " " LANGUAGE , " " --language " " LANGUAGE
Select
.BR deutsch ,
.BR english ,
.BR vietnamese ,
.BR chinese
or
.BR korean .
Common ISO aliases such as
.B de
and
.B en
are accepted.
.TP
.BR --middle-file " " FILE
Use an existing HTML middle table.  This avoids regenerating the expensive
.RB "reta -spalten --alles"
output.
.TP
.BR --middle-output " " FILE
Store the generated or supplied middle table in
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B --legacy-middle
Write the historical
.I ./middle.alx
intermediate file.
.TP
.BR --rows " " NUMBER
Generate only the first
.I NUMBER
data rows.  This option is intended for tests and previews.
.TP
.BR --data-dir " " DIRECTORY
Override the installed CSV directory.
.TP
.BR --asset-dir " " DIRECTORY
Override the installed asset directory.
.TP
.B --no-clobber
Fail if the file selected with
.B --output
already exists.
.TP
.BR -h , " " --help
Show command help.
.TP
.B --version
Show version information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RETA_DATA_DIR
CSV data directory.
.TP
.B RETA_ASSET_DIR
Static asset directory.
.TP
.B RETA_GENERATE_HTML_MIDDLE_FILE
Existing middle table; equivalent to
.BR --middle-file .
.TP
.B RETA_GENERATE_HTML_MIDDLE_OUTPUT
Path for an optional middle-table copy; equivalent to
.BR --middle-output .
.TP
.B RETA_GENERATE_HTML_ROWS
Preview row limit; equivalent to
.BR --rows .
.TP
.B RETA_GENERATE_HTML_BINARY
Override the private native executable, primarily for packaging tests.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/reta/csv
System CSV data for a distribution installation.
.TP
.I /usr/share/reta/assets
System HTML and catalog assets.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/reta/target/bin/generate-html-native
Default private executable for a
.I PREFIX=/usr
installation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Write to standard output:
.PP
.nf
generate_html > reta.html
.fi
.PP
Create an English page atomically:
.PP
.nf
generate_html --language english --output reta-en.html
.fi
.PP
Reuse a previously generated Python reference table:
.PP
.nf
generate_html --middle-file middle.alx --output reta.html
.fi
.PP
Keep an intermediate table explicitly:
.PP
.nf
generate_html --middle-output middle.alx > reta.html
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success.  Command-line errors use status 2, missing inputs use
66, output-creation failures use 73 and a missing native executable uses 127.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR reta (1)
